The batch id is one more field of the trace, so the tests above cover
it ([[TRACE]] holds one).  What is particular to it is where else it
goes: a reset keeps it in the reset record's trace and clears it, so
that a batch reset as a unit is no longer found under its id; a
snapshot of an agent's decision carries it as the screening's
[[batch]]; a screening recorded with a batch keeps it through a
save and a load; and in a spreadsheet-safe CSV the column is a text
column, so an id that starts like a formula gets its prefix.

