\subsection{Abstracts supplied by a service, and doubtful ones}
\label{sec:fetched-abstract}

An abstract that is not given by hand was supplied by a service, but
[[Paper.sources]] names the providers of the whole paper, not of each
field, so nothing said which one
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/287}).
That matters once a service's abstract field can hold something other
than an abstract (\cref{sec:doubtful-abstracts} in the enrichment
module): a reader who finds a disclosure statement where the abstract
should be wants to know where it came from.

[[scholar enrich]] knows: the outcome of each paper's lookups names the
source whose abstract it stored (\cref{sec:replace-doubtful-abstract}).
The record is kept where the record of a hand-given abstract is, on the
decision, in [[abstract_fetched]], and for the same reason
(\cref{sec:set-abstract}): a new paper field would need a rule of its
own in the three-way merge of paper metadata
(\cref{sec:session-integrity}) and in every merge of two copies of a
paper, to keep it paired with the abstract it describes, while a list
on the decision is saved, loaded, copied by an append and united by
the concurrent merge like the other histories.
It is not part of the decision's state, as [[abstract_set]] is not: it
changes no decision.

A record is [[{"at", "from", "chars", "digest", "replaced"}]]: when,
from which source, the length of the stored text and a digest of it,
and, when it replaced a doubtful abstract, that text with its reason
and source.
The record does not hold the abstract it describes, unlike a hand
record: enrichment stores abstracts for most papers of a session, and a
second copy of each would double the file.
The doubtful text it replaced is kept in full, in [[replaced]]: it is
no longer anywhere else, it may be what an earlier decision rested on,
and it is the way back when the new text belongs to another work (a
DOI lookup can return the wrong record); such replacements are few.
The digest is what lets a display tell whether the record still
describes the paper's abstract.
The abstract can change after the record without the record knowing:
a fold of two copies keeps one copy's abstract, a preprint adoption
brings the preprint's, a concurrent save takes another process's, a
hand-given text replaces it.
A record whose digest is not the abstract's then says nothing, rather
than name a source for a text it did not supply; so, for the same
reason, does every paper whose abstract was stored before records were
kept.
Searches do not record a source: a search's papers are merged across
providers before they reach the session, and which provider's abstract
the merged paper kept is not known there.

<<review data structures>>=
def abstract_digest(text: str) -> str:
    """A short digest of an abstract, to tell whether it changed."""
    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()[:16]


def note_fetched_abstract(
    decision: ReviewDecision,
    source: str,
    at: str,
    replaced: dict | None = None,
) -> dict | None:
    """Record that `source` supplied the abstract `decision`'s paper holds.

    `replaced` describes a doubtful abstract it replaced (`{"text",
    "reason", "from"}`). Returns the record, or None when the paper
    has no abstract.
    """
    abstract = decision.paper.abstract
    if not abstract:
        return None
    record = {
        "at": at,
        "from": source,
        "chars": len(abstract),
        "digest": abstract_digest(abstract),
        **({"replaced": replaced} if replaced else {}),
    }
    decision.add_fetched_abstract(record)
    return record


def fetched_abstract_source(decision: ReviewDecision) -> str | None:
    """The source that supplied the abstract the paper holds, if known.

    The newest record whose digest is the abstract's; None when none
    is (no record, or the abstract changed since).
    """
    abstract = decision.paper.abstract
    if not abstract:
        return None
    digest = abstract_digest(abstract)
    for record in reversed(decision.abstract_fetched):
        if record.get("digest") == digest:
            return record.get("from")
    return None
@

Which abstracts are doubtful is computed when asked, from the text,
not stored: the check is cheap, a stored flag would go stale when the
check is tuned, and sessions saved before it existed get it too.
[[abstract_doubt]] is the one place that applies the rule that an
abstract given by hand is never judged: while the paper still holds the
hand-given text ([[hand_abstract_replaced]] false), there is no doubt
to report.

<<review data structures>>=
def hand_given_abstract(decision: ReviewDecision) -> bool:
    """Whether the paper holds the abstract last given by hand."""
    return bool(decision.abstract_set) and not hand_abstract_replaced(
        decision
    )


def abstract_doubt(decision: ReviewDecision) -> str | None:
    """Why the paper's abstract looks like something else, or None.

    `doubtful_abstract` of the paper's abstract; None for an abstract
    given by hand, which is never judged.
    """
    if hand_given_abstract(decision):
        return None
    return doubtful_abstract(decision.paper.abstract)
