The list survives a save, a load and an append, and is written only
when there is one; malformed entries are written back as they were,
with one warning per file.  A save by a process that loaded the session
before a screening was recorded keeps it, and a screening run's save
keeps a decision another process saved meanwhile, in both orders.
Each process loads the session in a registry of its own, as in the
abstract tests above.

