The copies of an id beyond the first, which the lookup does not hold
(\cref{sec:review-create-strict}), join the session after the
conversion, unchanged.  Added before it, they would be in the
conversion's [[decision_lookup]], and a returned paper of their id
would merge into one of them through the branch for papers already in
the session, while the first copy, its id returned, would be neither
restored nor met.  After it, no returned paper meets them: it was
attached to the first copy.  They keep their order, so the save still
tells the copies apart by it.  A copy is told from the first by being
none of the decisions the lookup holds, not by its paper's id: the
conversion renames the papers of some decisions it meets (a name
written surname first, a homonym number), and a renamed first copy
looked up by its new id would be taken for one of the others and
added twice.

