\paragraph{A paper found again in the old decision store.}
\label{sec:decision-store-fallback}
When there is no session file, a paper's previous decision may be a
record of the old per-query store.  Until November 2026 its decision
was rebuilt around the copy the search returned alone, with only the
search's provider, which dropped the abstract, venue, URL and PDF link
that the record holds
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/194}): the same loss as
a session file's decision suffered before [[stored_paper_with]]
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/192}).  So the record's
paper is rebuilt as the restore does ([[paper_from_decision_record]])
and goes through the same rule as a session file's paper: the stored
values win, the returned copy fills the gaps, and a DOI-less record met
by a DOI copy found under its legacy hash id lets the DOI copy keep its
identity and version fields ([[merge_version_of]]).  The provider names
both the record's provider and the search's ([[united_providers]]).

The record's decision becomes the returned paper's in the same way:
its status, tags, source, example flag and confidence, with the paper
built as above ([[decision_from_record]]).  (The restore of papers not
returned, above, reads the same fields in code of its own.)

<<review session functions>>=
def decision_from_record(
    record: Any, paper: Paper, provider: str
) -> ReviewDecision:
    """The decision of a record of the old per-query decision store.

    `record` is a `notes.ReviewDecisionRecord`; the decision gets its
    status, tags, source, example flag and LLM confidence, and the
    given `paper` and `provider`.  An unknown status reads as pending.
    An unknown source string is kept, as `ReviewSource` keeps one from
    a session file (`is_unknown`); a source that is not a string reads
    as human.
    """
    status = DecisionStatus.PENDING
    if record.status == "kept":
        status = DecisionStatus.KEPT
    elif record.status == "discarded":
        status = DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
    source = ReviewSource.HUMAN
    try:
        source = ReviewSource(getattr(record, "source", "human"))
    except ValueError:
        pass
    return ReviewDecision(
        paper=paper,
        provider=provider,
        status=status,
        tags=extract_tags_from_record(record),
        source=source,
        is_example=getattr(record, "is_example", False),
        llm_confidence=getattr(record, "llm_confidence", None),
    )
@

The source is kept as stored, as a session file's is
(\cref{sec:review-source}): a record of a source this version does not
know keeps its value and counts as unreviewed, never as a human's.

