A namesake's record (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/203})
is tested in both of its forms with the same stored record, a discarded
work from 1994, and a work of 2014 with the same title and first author
returned by the re-run.  With a DOI, the work of 2014 meets the record
under its legacy hash id: it must come out pending, without the
record's tags and with the search's link, while the record is restored
beside it with its own decision and no link.  Without a DOI, it meets
the record under its own id: the session then holds the record's
decision only, with the record's paper, and the newcomer in
[[same_id_copies]].  The second form is run also with a record that
holds a DOI under the hash key, whose rebuilt paper has another id than
its key.  Last, the rules must not cost a paper that is one work with
the record its decision: a year apart, under either id, the decision is
taken over, link included, and the session holds that one decision,
not a restored copy of the record beside it
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/211}).  So also for
the record of an arXiv preprint, from whose URL the record's paper
derives an arXiv DOI, met by its published version with another DOI;
and under the paper's own DOI, twenty years apart, though the record's
paper then fills nothing.

