The case of \url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/164}: the
default search merges OpenAlex, which answered, with DBLP, which
failed.  The session must hold two records with their own outcomes, the
paper only OpenAlex returned must link to OpenAlex alone, and a merged
record already in the session from before, of providers this run does
not all cover, must load and stay as it was (one that the run covers is
superseded, \cref{sec:superseded-merged}; this test used OpenAlex and
DBLP before that rule existed).
The merge is the real [[SearchResult.merge]] that the search command
runs.

