Copies fold when their verdicts are equal ([[decision_verdict]]), so
two copies a human decided alike can carry two records of the review.
The survivor keeps the newer one, by [[human_decided_at]]: it is the
latest moment a human looked at the work, which is what the record of
the decision that stands should say, and a copy with a record beats one
without, so a fold never loses the evidence that a human decided.

<<review session functions>>=
def newer_human_record(
    first: ReviewDecision, second: ReviewDecision
) -> ReviewDecision:
    """The one of two decisions whose human review record is newer.

    A decision with a record beats one without; on equal times (or two
    without a record) `first`.
    """
    def key(decision):
        at = decision.human_decided_at
        if at is None:
            return (False, float("-inf"), "")
        try:
            return (True, datetime.fromisoformat(at).timestamp(), at)
        except ValueError:
            return (True, float("-inf"), at)

    return second if key(second) > key(first) else first
