Two decisions under one id must also outlast what comes after them
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/228}).  The session
file holds the pair of the renamed Scopus probe above: the work
discarded as found by OpenAlex, and kept as found by Scopus, the
latter with the link of its search.  An append that does not return the
work keeps both, and so does one that returns it, which attaches the
returned paper to the first copy only: its provider and link, none of
them on the second.  Then the save: two session objects loaded from the
file, one changes a copy and saves, the other saves untouched; the
file must keep that change, on that copy, whichever of the two it is,
and the links of one copy must not pass to the other.  Last, the save's
guard against lost decisions: resetting the second copy to pending,
beside a first copy that is pending already, is this process's own
reset and no loss to warn about.

