\paragraph{The cost of pairing.}
\label{sec:pairing-cost}
The loaded copies gone from here were first found by reading the whole
baseline for every paper id in the file, so a save cost time in the
square of the session's size
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/316}).
Under cProfile, a save of 10\,000 decisions took 37.7\,s, 24.9\,s of
them in the pairing (\cref{sec:save-cost}).
The baseline's keys are therefore grouped by paper id once per save,
in the baseline's order, which is the order the scan visited them in;
each id then reads only its own keys, and the rules above see the same
keys in the same order.

