The rules must give exactly the pairs they gave before, so the tests
keep the pairing as it was, the scan included, as a reference
([[reference_pair_with_file]], copied from the version before this
change and not to be changed with the rules), and compare the two in
two ways.  First, every scenario the tests of copies under one id build
(\cref{sec:session-copies}) runs again with [[pair_with_file]] replaced
by a check that calls both and compares their pairs and additions, by
identity.  Second, a generator with a fixed seed (316) builds a few
hundred pairs of sessions, ours and the file, from one loaded state:
few papers, so that copies under one id are common, and on each side a
few random changes of the kinds the scenarios name (renames, drops,
inserts, swaps, changed decisions and links, folds), sometimes without
a baseline.

