The error is meant to be read once and acted on, so it is one sentence
per fact: the file, why it was not written, that nothing was written,
and where this process's session is with the command that merges it
in, or that it could not be kept, or, for a command that had changed
nothing yet, to run it again.  The path in the command is quoted for
the shell, so that it can be pasted.  The cause decides the words and
the exit status: [[held]] (another process holds the lock),
[[lock-file]] (the lock file cannot be opened) or [[interrupted]].

<<review constants>>=
SAVE_REFUSALS = {
    "held": "is locked by another scholar process ({reason})",
    "lock-file": "cannot be locked ({reason}; check its permissions)",
    "interrupted": "was not locked: the wait for its lock was interrupted",
}
SAVE_RETRY_WHEN = {
    "held": "once the other scholar process has finished",
    "lock-file": "once its lock file can be opened",
    "interrupted": "once the other scholar process has finished",
}
