The kept file is named [[<name>.json.unsaved-<UTC time>-<random>]],
made by [[tempfile.mkstemp]] as the caches' files beside an unreadable
cache are (\cref{sec:cache-concurrency}): the name is created
exclusively, so two refused saves never share one, and the time sorts
the files by age.  The name does not end in [[.json]], so no listing of
sessions reads it as a session; [[sessions list]] names it instead.
It holds the object a save would have written ([[session_file_data]])
and, under [[UNSAVED_KEY]], what a merge needs besides: the name of the
session file, and the baseline with each decision's key in it
(\cref{sec:copies-in-the-merge}), since a merge must know what this
process changed and what it found as loaded.  Without the kept file the
recovery would be to run the command again, which for a TUI review
means the review.

