An interrupted keep leaves no file: an interrupt while the session is
serialised comes before the file exists, and an interrupt that stops
the keep (where it cannot be held back) gives the one line that says
the session is lost.  The case of two real interrupts, the second held
back, is tested through the command line (\cref{sec:sessions-recover}).

