The counts are printed by the commands that select a tier, in the same
words everywhere ([[tier_lines]]).  [[noun]] names what the papers are
(\enquote{pending papers}, \enquote{papers}), and the rule is spelled
as the options that gave it, so a line can be quoted with its command.

<<review filtering functions>>=
def tier_lines(tier: TierSelection, noun: str = "papers") -> list[str]:
    """The tier's counts as lines of text, the selection first."""
    rule = tier.rule
    labels = {
        "top": f"--top {rule.top} (a place at most {rule.top} in a "
               "relevance-ordered answer)",
        "min_providers": f"--min-providers {rule.min_providers} "
                         f"(returned by at least {rule.min_providers} "
                         "databases)",
        "provider": "--provider " + ", ".join(rule.providers) + (
            f" --query-like {rule.query_like!r}"
            if rule.query_like else ""
        ),
    }
    lines = [
        f"Tier: {len(tier.decisions)} of {tier.total} {noun} selected, "
        f"{tier.not_selected} not selected."
    ]
    for name in rule.conditions():
        lines.append(
            f"  {labels[name]}: {tier.met[name]} "
            f"({tier.only[name]} by this condition alone)"
        )
    if len(rule.conditions()) > 1:
        lines.append(f"  by more than one condition: {tier.several}")
    lines.append(
        f"  place unknown (no place recorded): {tier.place_unknown}; "
        "placed only in answers not ordered by relevance: "
        f"{tier.no_relevance_place}; databases unknown (only merged "
        f"records or old links): {tier.databases_unknown}"
    )
    return lines
@

To plan a screen, a user needs two numbers before choosing a rule: how
many pending papers a place cut would select and how many several
databases would.  [[sessions show]] prints them in one line
([[tier_overview_line]]) for one place and one number of databases,
[[TIER_SHOW_TOP]] and [[TIER_SHOW_PROVIDERS]], named once here.  The
line appears only when some link holds a place, so a session from
before places were kept shows what it always showed.  When none of the
pending papers has a relevance place (a session searched only by
answers ordered otherwise, such as Semantic Scholar's unlimited bulk
search, \cref{sec:search-result-order} in the [[scholar]] module), the
line says so rather than reporting a bare zero, which would read as
\enquote{the head of the answers holds nothing}.

<<review constants>>=
TIER_SHOW_TOP = 100
TIER_SHOW_PROVIDERS = 3
<<review filtering functions>>=
def tier_overview_line(session: "ReviewSession") -> str | None:
    """How many pending papers a place cut and a database count select.

    `None` when no link of the session holds a place.
    """
    if not any(
        link_rank(link) is not None
        for decision in session.decisions for link in decision.found_by
    ):
        return None
    records = LinkedRecords(session)
    pending = pending_papers(session)
    places = [relevance_place(d, records) for d in pending]
    within = sum(1 for p in places if p is not None and p <= TIER_SHOW_TOP)
    several = sum(
        1 for d in pending
        if len(returning_databases(d, records)) >= TIER_SHOW_PROVIDERS
    )
    by_place = (
        f"{within} within the first {TIER_SHOW_TOP} places of a "
        "relevance-ordered answer"
        if any(p is not None for p in places) or not pending
        else "none placed in a relevance-ordered answer"
    )
    return (
        f"Screening tier: of {len(pending)} pending papers, {by_place}, "
        f"{several} returned by {TIER_SHOW_PROVIDERS} or more databases."
    )
