The check is computed whenever a session is shown, over every decision
with a reason, and a screened session can hold 30\,000 of them.  For
scale: 30\,000 synthetic decisions with two reasons each took 3.0 to
4.4\,s of processor time in a review of this change, on a machine under
heavy load from parallel test runs; that is a measurement, not a
promise.  The test below is a guard against a regression, not a
benchmark.  It times 10\,000 decisions with a quoted reason and an
abstract of 400 words holding a dash and a pair of quote marks, in
processor time, which waiting for a busy processor does not add to.
The current folding took about 1.8\,s there, under load; folding with
[[str.translate]], which was about fifty times slower on one abstract
(above), took about 15\,s for the whole check.  The limit lies between
the two, with room for a busy machine.

