A rule applied with one [[--reason]] counts once in the session-wide
pool, but it counts: the same reason repeated over many runs adds up.
Three shapes show it.  An agent that records one paper per call (15
runs of one row, one reason) shares that reason over 15 records;
three runs of eight records on one reason are three applications of a
rule, three records in the pool and no finding, while twelve such runs
are twelve; and a run of 300 on one reason with nine more rows of that
reason in another run makes ten.

