The rows above say how many decisions an agent made, not whether
each of them can be checked.  An agent that recorded no reason
([[agent_reason]], \cref{sec:agent-audit-fields}) left a verdict that
nobody can check record by record, so after the summary one sentence
says how many of the agent's decisions carry a reason and how many do
not.  A decision an agent made and a human then reviewed counts too,
since its reason is still what the review was measured against.  The
report is written in English only (unlike the audit table), so the
sentence is too, and it is left out when no agent decided anything.

<<review report generation>>=
def agent_reasons_sentence(decisions) -> str:
    """One sentence counting the agent's decisions with a recorded reason.

    Empty when no agent decided anything.
    """
    agents = (ReviewSource.AGENT_UNREVIEWED, ReviewSource.AGENT_REVIEWED)
    made = [d for d in decisions if d.is_decided and d.source in agents]
    if not made:
        return ""
    reasoned = sum(1 for d in made if d.agent_reason)
    silent = len(made) - reasoned
    decisions_word = "decision" if len(made) == 1 else "decisions"
    record = "records" if reasoned == 1 else "record"
    do = "does" if silent == 1 else "do"
    return (
        f"Of the {len(made)} {decisions_word} an agent made, "
        f"{reasoned} {record} the agent's reason and {silent} {do} not."
    )
