A reason can also be checked against its record: the quotes in it
should be the record's own words (\cref{sec:reason-quotes}).  The report
states, after the agent's reasons, how many machine reasons quote the
record and how many hold a quote that is not in its title or abstract,
the agent's and the classifier's apart, since they come from different
screeners and a reader weighs them differently.  The sentence counts
every reason the session holds, including those of decisions a human
has since reviewed, as [[sessions show]] does, and it is left out when
the session holds no machine reason.  It counts and does not list: the
quotes are in [[sessions show]], and a report is not the place to
correct a screen.

<<review report generation>>=
def reason_quotes_sentence(decisions) -> str:
    """One sentence with the quote check of the machine reasons.

    Empty when no decision carries an agent's or a classifier's reason.
    """
    tally = quote_check_tally(reason_quote_checks(d) for d in decisions)
    clauses = []
    for kind, label in (("agent", "agent"), ("llm", "classifier")):
        counts = tally[kind]
        if not counts["reasons"]:
            continue
        reasons = "reason" if counts["reasons"] == 1 else "reasons"
        hold = "holds" if counts["checked"] == 1 else "hold"
        clauses.append(
            f"of {counts['reasons']} {label} {reasons}, "
            f"{counts['checked']} {hold} such a quote and "
            f"{counts['unmatched']} a quote not found in the record"
        )
    if not clauses:
        return ""
    return (
        f"Quotes of at least {MIN_QUOTE_WORDS} words in the machine "
        "reasons were compared with each record's title and abstract: "
        + "; ".join(clauses) + "."
    )
