A decision made on a record without an abstract rests on its title,
and the reader of the report should know how many did
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/293}).  One sentence
after the summary counts the decided papers without an abstract and
splits them by what the last [[scholar enrich]] found for them
([[abstract_gap]], \cref{sec:abstract-lookup}): every source asked had
none, nothing could be asked, a lookup failed, or there is no record of
a lookup, which is what every session written before the record existed
holds.  Decided papers whose abstract is doubtful
(\cref{sec:fetched-abstract}) are added at the end.  [[sessions show]]
prints the same sentence.  Nothing is said when every decided paper
has an abstract and none is doubtful.  The count is of the papers
as they stand: an abstract filled in after the decision makes the paper
count as having one, although the screener did not see it, since the
session does not record what a screener saw.

<<review report generation>>=
def decided_without_abstract_sentence(decisions) -> str:
    """One sentence counting the decided papers without an abstract.

    Empty when there are none.
    """
    gap = abstract_gap(d for d in decisions if d.is_decided)
    if not gap.without and not gap.doubtful:
        return ""
    if not gap.without:
        return (
            f"{gap.doubtful} of the {gap.papers} decided papers "
            f"{'was' if gap.doubtful == 1 else 'were'} decided on a "
            "doubtful abstract."
        )
    parts = abstract_gap_parts(gap)
    return (
        f"{gap.without} of the {gap.papers} decided papers "
        f"{'was' if gap.without == 1 else 'were'} decided without an "
        f"abstract ({'; '.join(parts)})"
        + (f", and {gap.doubtful} on a doubtful one" if gap.doubtful
           else "")
        + "."
    )
