Kept papers are grouped by theme and discarded papers by motivation, one
list per tag. A paper with several tags appears under each of them; that
repetition is intended, because a reader looking up one theme should see
everything filed under it. Without tags the papers form a single list.

Each entry carries the mark of an unreviewed machine decision
([[unreviewed_mark]], \cref{sec:review-source}) after the citation.  The
lists are where a reader of the report meets the papers one by one, and
a paper an agent kept without anyone reading it must not look like one
the author screened.

