Three facts about how decisions are recorded shape the cited rule.
First, [[sessions decide -t]] appends to a row's tags, so a human who
keeps an LLM-classified [[supports-claim]] paper under a theme leaves
both tags on it; looking only at the first tag would file the paper
under the category and count no cited rows at all. The rule therefore
splits the tags into category tags, note tags and theme tags and takes
the theme from the last group. Second, an LLM keep is a candidate, not
a citation, and so is an agent's: only a decision a human made (or
reviewed) counts as cited, which is also what the [[decision_source]]
column of the CSV export says. The test is
[[ReviewSource.is_unreviewed]] (\cref{sec:review-source}), so the two
machine sources cannot drift apart. Third, when the caller names its themes with [[--theme]], that
list is an allowlist: any other tag that is neither a category nor a
known note is shown as a note, so a stray tag cannot pass for a theme.
Without the list, every tag that is not a category or a note is a
theme. Notes are appended in parentheses to whatever reason the row
has; a row with only notes is filed among the \enquote{other} rows.

When a row carries several category tags, the \emph{last} one is the
decision: tags accumulate in the order they were given, so a reviewer
who changes an LLM's \enquote{supports} to \enquote{false hit} leaves
both, and taking the first once counted an explicitly rejected paper as
supporting evidence in a published appendix. The confidence is shown
for the rows whose category is the machine's: unreviewed LLM or agent
decisions and the ones a human confirmed as they stood. A human who changed the
decision owns the new label, so no confidence goes with it. Finally, a
theme that merely repeats the word \enquote{cited} adds nothing and is
not repeated.

The caption promises a confidence for every machine-classified row, so
such a row recorded without one---[[sessions decide --source llm]]
without [[--confidence]], or a session from before the classifier
stored it---says so with a localised \enquote{n/a} instead of looking
like a human row. An empty cell would be read as \enquote{nobody
asked}, which is exactly what the reader cannot check.

Whose confidence it is depends on who classified the row, and the
caption must say so: a table whose rows an agent decided used to read
\enquote{the model's confidence is given} where no model was involved
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/262}).  So
[[audit_reason_and_confidence]] also returns the origin of the number
when the label shows one, [[AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_LLM]] or
[[AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_AGENT]], and the caption picks its sentence from the
origins of the rows it lists (\cref{sec:audit-confidence-sentence}).
A row a human confirmed keeps its machine origin, since the number is
still the machine's.  A decision of unknown source (a hand-edited
value) shows the confidence like an unreviewed one; nothing records
who made it, and the number sits in the classifier's field
([[llm_confidence]]), so it counts as the model's, which is what the
caption said of it before.  [[audit_reason]] keeps its two-item result
for its many callers and drops the origin.

The category is the classification, but the status is the decision,
and the decision wins (issue~\#89). A row whose final status is
discarded is never listed as cited, supporting or qualifying, whatever
its category says: the reviewer, or the model, looked at the paper and
excluded it, and counting it as evidence for the claim in a published
appendix is exactly the mistake the issue reported. Such a row keeps
its category in the reason, marked as excluded, but sorts among the
\enquote{other} rows, so [[--bearing-only]] never lists it and the
caption counts it separately. The adjacent and off-topic categories do
not bear on the claim, so a discarded row there is simply what it says.

Which tags a row shows as notes is decided in one place,
[[audit_note_tags]], because a second reader needs the same answer: the
work merge lends the notes of a work's other copies to the row that
represents it (\cref{sec:audit-row-notes}), and it must lend exactly
what each copy's own row would show.  The notes are a decision's note
tags and, with [[--theme]], its stray tags.  A pending decision shows
them as well, after the pending label: a note records a fact about the
work, such as \enquote{recorded, not cited}, which holds before anyone
has classified the record, and a pending row that hid it hid the fact.
A discard under an exclusion criterion shows none, since its reason is
the criterion alone and its other tags are the earlier criteria the
reviewer replaced.  The notes lent by other copies reach
[[audit_reason]] as [[also_notes]].

<<review imports>>=
from collections.abc import Collection, Sequence
<<review report generation>>=
def audit_category(tags: list[str]) -> str | None:
    """Return the deciding (last) audit category among `tags`, if any."""
    return next((t for t in reversed(tags) if t in AUDIT_CATEGORIES), None)


def audit_excluded(decision: ReviewDecision) -> bool:
    """Tell whether a bearing category was overruled by a discard."""
    category = audit_category(decision.tags)
    return (
        decision.status == DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
        and category is not None
        and AUDIT_CATEGORIES[category] <= AUDIT_ORDER_BEARING
    )


def audit_note_tags(
    decision: ReviewDecision,
    *,
    theme_names: dict[str, str],
    notes: dict[str, str],
) -> list[str]:
    """Return the tags `decision`'s own row shows as notes, known first.

    Those are its note tags and, when the caller named its themes, every
    other tag that is neither a category nor a theme.  A discard under
    an exclusion criterion shows none: its reason is the criterion alone.
    """
    tags = decision.tags
    if audit_exclusion_criterion(
        decision, theme_names=theme_names, notes=notes
    ) is not None:
        return []
    noted = [t for t in tags if t in notes]
    if theme_names:
        noted += [
            t for t in tags
            if t not in AUDIT_CATEGORIES and t not in notes
            and t not in theme_names
        ]
    return noted


def audit_note_text(tag: str, notes: dict[str, str]) -> str:
    """Return how the audit table writes the note `tag`."""
    return notes[tag] if tag in notes else escape_latex(tag)


AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_LLM = "llm"
AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_AGENT = "agent"


def audit_confidence_origin(source: ReviewSource) -> str:
    """Return who gave the confidence of a machine decision of `source`."""
    if source in (ReviewSource.AGENT_UNREVIEWED, ReviewSource.AGENT_REVIEWED):
        return AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_AGENT
    return AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_LLM


def audit_with_notes(label: str, texts: list[str]) -> str:
    """Append the note `texts` to `label` in parentheses, if any."""
    return f"{label} ({'; '.join(texts)})" if texts else label


def audit_reason(
    decision: ReviewDecision,
    *,
    theme_names: dict[str, str],
    strings: dict,
    also_notes: Sequence[str] = (),
    cited: bool | None = None,
) -> tuple[str, int]:
    """Return the reason label and sort order for `decision`.

    `also_notes` are note tags of the work's other copies; they are
    added to the label's notes, after the decision's own, each once.
    `cited` says whether the text cites the work (`--cited-from`); with
    None a keep is cited when a human made or confirmed it.
    """
    label, order, _ = audit_reason_and_confidence(
        decision, theme_names=theme_names, strings=strings,
        also_notes=also_notes, cited=cited,
    )
    return label, order


def audit_reason_and_confidence(
    decision: ReviewDecision,
    *,
    theme_names: dict[str, str],
    strings: dict,
    also_notes: Sequence[str] = (),
    cited: bool | None = None,
) -> tuple[str, int, str | None]:
    """Return the reason label, the sort order and who gave the confidence.

    The third item is `AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_LLM` or `AUDIT_CONFIDENCE_AGENT`
    when the label shows a confidence (or its placeholder), else None.
    """
    tags = list(decision.tags)
    notes = strings["notes"]
    category = audit_category(tags)
    own_notes = audit_note_tags(
        decision, theme_names=theme_names, notes=notes
    )
    note_texts = [audit_note_text(t, notes) for t in own_notes]
    <<add the notes of the work's other copies>>
    if theme_names:
        theme_tags = [t for t in tags if t in theme_names]
    else:
        theme_tags = [
            t for t in tags if t not in AUDIT_CATEGORIES and t not in notes
        ]
    human_decision = not decision.source.is_unreviewed
    kept = decision.status == DecisionStatus.KEPT
    machine_label = decision.source.is_unreviewed or (
        decision.source.is_machine and not decision.is_example
    )
    confidence = ""
    if machine_label and decision.llm_confidence is not None:
        confidence = (
            f" ({audit_number(decision.llm_confidence, strings, 2)})"
        )
    elif machine_label:
        confidence = f" ({strings['no_confidence']})"
    origin = audit_confidence_origin(decision.source)

    criterion = audit_exclusion_criterion(
        decision, theme_names=theme_names, notes=notes
    )
    by_screening = cited is None

    <<label a work by whether the text cites it>>
    if decision.status == DecisionStatus.PENDING:
        return audit_with_notes(strings["pending"], note_texts), \
            AUDIT_ORDER_PENDING, None
    shown = None
    if kept and human_decision and by_screening and theme_tags:
        theme = theme_names.get(theme_tags[0], theme_tags[0])
        label = f"\\emph{{{strings['cited']}}}"
        if theme.casefold() != strings["cited"].casefold():
            label += ": " + escape_latex(theme)
        order = AUDIT_ORDER_CITED
    elif kept and human_decision and by_screening and not tags:
        label, order = f"\\emph{{{strings['cited']}}}", AUDIT_ORDER_CITED
    elif audit_excluded(decision):
        label = f"{strings[category]}{confidence}, {strings['excluded']}"
        order, shown = AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER, confidence
    elif category is not None:
        label = strings[category] + confidence
        order, shown = AUDIT_CATEGORIES[category], confidence
    elif audit_uncited_keep(decision, cited):
        <<label a keep the text does not cite>>
    elif criterion is not None:
        label = escape_latex(criterion) + confidence
        order, shown = AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER, confidence
    elif own_notes:
        return "; ".join(note_texts), AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER, None
    elif not tags:
        return audit_with_notes(strings["pending"], note_texts), \
            AUDIT_ORDER_PENDING, None
    else:
        label = escape_latex(tags[0]) + confidence
        order, shown = AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER, confidence
    return audit_with_notes(label, note_texts), order, \
        origin if shown else None
@

Each category, the confidence suffix and the fall-through cases are
checked in turn:

