The first test is the case of issue~\#204, with the human copy both
second and first, so the result cannot come from the order of the
decisions.  Confirmed machine sources count as confirmed, an unknown
source, an unreviewed agent and a pending copy do not, and the
confirmed keep wins
also against a stronger unreviewed category.  The discard tests
follow the paragraphs above: a confirmed discard of the work wins,
also the exclusion of a qualifying work, which then stays out of the
[[--bearing-only]] table, and a discard under a topical criterion;
a discard of the record does not, nor one whose criterion is
[[no-abstract]] only because a named theme is skipped; equal
order goes to the confirmed copy, in the first tier by the tiers
and in the second by the third part of the key; and
between two confirmed decisions the order decides.

