    wanted = entry_edition(readings, edition[0] if edition else None)
    if wanted is not None and not any(
        loose_title(entry[1].paper.title)[1] == wanted for entry in found
    ):
        if loose_index is None:
            loose_index = _loose_title_index(session)
        preferred = match_loose_title(
            key, readings, edition[0] if edition else None, loose_index,
            same_edition=True,
        )
        if preferred.works:
            cited.append(preferred)
            continue
@

The rules for what is set aside are pinned on titles first: the
edition phrases in their several spellings, the editions a field can
give, and the titles that must stay whole even on a record without
authors: mixed-case titles that start with a number, a title that is
only an edition phrase, an edition word inside a title, an edition
that is the title's object, and a number before a heading in a script
without case.  A heading in capitals keeps its number on a record with
authors.

