\paragraph{Where the text and the screening disagree.}
Two kinds of entry need the author's attention, and the table alone
does not show either clearly enough.  The text may cite a work whose
row the session excludes, whatever the reason: the row then carries
the note \enquote{cited in the text}, but in a table of a thousand rows
a note is easily missed, and the author should decide whether the
exclusion or the citation is wrong.  And the text may cite a work the
session does not hold at all: it has no row, so the table cannot show
it.  [[cited_text_disagreements]] returns both lists, from the same
rows the table is built from; the command prints them on standard
error.  They are not counted in the caption, which counts only what
the table shows.

<<review report generation>>=
def cited_text_disagreements(
    session: ReviewSession,
    entries: Sequence[CitedEntry],
    *,
    theme_names: dict[str, str],
    strings: dict,
) -> tuple[list[CitedEntry], list[CitedEntry]]:
    """Split off the cited entries the session excludes or lacks.

    Returns `(excluded, not_held)`: entries one of whose rows is
    discarded, and entries that matched no decision.
    """
    rows = collect_audit_rows(
        session, theme_names=theme_names, strings=strings,
        cited_works={work for entry in entries for work in entry.works},
    )
    status = {row.work: row.status for row in rows}
    excluded = [
        entry for entry in entries
        if any(status.get(work) == DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
               for work in entry.works)
    ]
    not_held = [entry for entry in entries if not entry.works]
    return excluded, not_held
@

The session holds the cases of the issue and of the matching rules:
an agent's keep of a work cited by DOI, a human's keep of a work cited
by title, a human's keep the text does not cite, a human's discard of a
cited work, a preprint the session adopted for a published version the
text cites, a namesake of a cited work ten years older, and a work with
a DOI other than the entry's.  The bibliography also cites one work the
session does not hold.

<<test functions>>=
def _cited_session():
  session = ReviewSession(
    query="q", providers=["openalex"], timestamp=datetime.now(),
    name="cited",
  )
  agent, human = ReviewSource.AGENT_UNREVIEWED, ReviewSource.HUMAN
  kept, discarded = DecisionStatus.KEPT, DecisionStatus.DISCARDED

  def decision(title, author, year, status, tags, source=human,
               conf=None, **paper):
    return ReviewDecision(
      paper=Paper(title=title, authors=[author], year=year, **paper),
      provider="openalex", status=status, tags=tags, source=source,
      llm_confidence=conf,
    )

  session.decisions = [
    decision("Agent kept", "Ann Ash", 2020, kept, ["ml"], agent, 0.8,
             doi="10.1/agent"),
    decision("Human kept, cited", "Bo Berg", 2021, kept, ["ml"]),
    decision("Human kept, not cited", "Cy Cole", 2022, kept, ["ml"]),
    decision("Human discarded", "Di Dahl", 2019, discarded,
             ["off-topic-false-hit"], doi="10.1/disc"),
    decision("A preprint", "Ed Ek", 2023, kept, ["supports-claim"],
             agent, 0.9, doi="10.48550/arXiv.2301.00001",
             published_versions=[{"doi": "10.1/pub",
                                   "relation": "preprint-of"}]),
    decision("Editorial", "Fy Fors", 2000, kept, ["ml"]),
    decision("Other DOI", "Gu Gran", 2020, kept, ["ml"], doi="10.1/held"),
  ]
  return session


def _cited_entries():
  return [(key, [paper]) for key, paper in _cited_papers()]


def _cited_papers():
  return [
    ("ash2020", Paper(title="Something else", authors=["Ann Ash"],
                      year=2020, doi="https://doi.org/10.1/AGENT")),
    ("berg2021", Paper(title="Human Kept, Cited", authors=["Berg, Bo"],
                       year=2021)),
    ("dahl2019", Paper(title="Human discarded", authors=["Di Dahl"],
                       year=2019, doi="10.1/disc")),
    ("ek2024", Paper(title="The published version", authors=["Ed Ek"],
                     year=2024, doi="10.1/pub")),
    ("fors2010", Paper(title="Editorial", authors=["Fy Fors"],
                       year=2010)),
    ("gran2020", Paper(title="Other DOI", authors=["Gu Gran"],
                       year=2020, doi="10.1/cited")),
  ]


