\subsection{CSV report}

The CSV carries every field the other artefacts summarise, including the
LLM provenance columns, so that a spreadsheet or a script can recompute
any of the tables above. The last column is the session's paper id, the
selector [[sessions decide --paper-id]] accepts, so a record without a
DOI can be decided from the CSV without opening the TUI.
The review columns ([[llm_review_outcome]], [[llm_change_direction]])
describe how a human handled a machine decision and apply to the agent's
decisions as much as to the LLM's; their names predate the agent source,
and [[decision_source]] says which machine it was.
[[source_relabelled]] lists the corrections of the source
(\cref{sec:relabel-source}) as [[from->to time]] (with
[[by NAME]] when the record names who), separated by
semicolons, so that a spreadsheet that counts sources can see which of
them were set after the decision, and from what.  [[reset_from]]
lists the decisions the record had before it was set back to pending
(\cref{sec:reset-decision}) as [[status by source time]] (again with
[[by NAME]]), so that a row that is pending, or decided anew, still
shows what the earlier screen said.
[[agent_reason]], [[agent_by]], [[agent_decided_at]] and
[[agent_batch]] are the agent's trace (\cref{sec:agent-audit-fields}),
empty when not recorded, so that a spreadsheet can check an agent's verdicts
record by record as it can read the classifier's confidence.  They go
before [[reset_from]]; [[paper_id]] stays last.
The classifier's own trace (\cref{sec:llm-audit-fields}) comes right
before them, one column per field of [[LLM_AUDIT_FIELDS]] in that
order: the model, the time, the prompt version, the reason and whether
the abstract was cut.  Each trace is kept whole in its own columns,
not merged into one reason column, since a decision an agent corrected
with [[--keep-trace]] holds the classifier's reason and the agent's
side by side, and a reader must tell them apart.  The truncation flag
is written [[true]] or [[false]]: under the [[value or ""]] rule of the
agent's columns [[False]] would become an empty cell, and an empty cell
here means that the flag was never recorded.
[[best_rank]] and [[providers_count]] follow [[provider]], since they
say more about the searches that returned the paper: the paper's best
place in a relevance-ordered answer of a current search
([[relevance_place]], empty when none is known) and the number of
databases whose current searches returned it ([[returning_databases]];
the column keeps the option's name, [[--min-providers]]),
the two numbers a screening tier is selected by
(\cref{sec:screening-tier}).  A spreadsheet can then sort and filter by
them, as a tier would.  Both are numbers, and the spreadsheet-safe
writer treats them as such.
[[abstract_from]] says where each abstract given by hand was found
(\cref{sec:set-abstract}), as [[from time]] (with [[by NAME]]),
separated by semicolons, so that a spreadsheet that reads the
[[abstract]] column can tell a provider's text from one a screener
found; it goes after [[reset_from]], before [[paper_id]].
The cells hold the stored text as it is, also when it begins like a
formula; [[spreadsheet_safe=True]] (the export's
[[--spreadsheet-safe]]) writes a copy for opening in a spreadsheet
program instead (\cref{sec:spreadsheet-safe}).

<<review report generation>>=
def generate_csv_report(
    session: ReviewSession, output_path: Path, spreadsheet_safe: bool = False
) -> None:
    """
    Generate a CSV report of the review session.

    The CSV includes all papers (kept and discarded) with columns:
    - status: kept/discarded/pending
    - title, authors, year, venue, doi, url
    - tags: semicolon-separated list of themes/motivations
    - abstract: full abstract text
    - provider: search provider that returned the paper
    - best_rank: the paper's best place in a relevance-ordered answer
      of a current search, empty when none is known
    - providers_count: how many databases' current searches returned it
      (providers sharing a quota group are one database)
    - decision_source: where the keep/discard decision originated
    - llm_confidence: 0.0-1.0 confidence for LLM decisions (if available)
    - llm_review_outcome: human/unreviewed/confirmed/changed (for LLM
      and agent decisions alike; `decision_source` tells them apart)
    - llm_change_direction: kept->discarded or discarded->kept (only for changed)
    - source_relabelled: each correction of the source, as
      `from->to time [by NAME]`
    - llm_model, llm_decided_at, llm_prompt_version, llm_reason,
      llm_abstract_truncated: the classifier's trace as `scholar llm
      classify` stored it (`true`/`false` for the flag), empty when
      unknown
    - agent_reason, agent_by, agent_decided_at, agent_batch: the
      reason an agent gave with `sessions decide --reason`, who gave
      it, when, and the batch it came from
    - human_decided_at, human_decided_via, human_by: the record of a
      human's review (when, `tui` or `decide`, who as given); empty
      for a decision without a record of the review
    - reset_from: each earlier decision the record was reset from, as
      `status by source time [by NAME]`
    - abstract_from: where each abstract given by hand was found, as
      `from time [by NAME]`

    Args:
        session: The ReviewSession to report on.
        output_path: Path for the .csv file.
        spreadsheet_safe: Write every text cell through
            `spreadsheet_safe_cell`, so that a spreadsheet program does
            not read it as a formula; a number in `year` or
            `llm_confidence` is written as it is. Off by default: the
            raw file is the one for scripts.
    """
    import csv

    def llm_review_outcome(decision: ReviewDecision) -> str:
        if decision.source == ReviewSource.HUMAN:
            return "human"
        if decision.source.is_unreviewed:
            return "unreviewed"
        return "changed" if decision.is_example else "confirmed"

    def classifier_cell(value) -> str:
        if isinstance(value, bool):
            return "true" if value else "false"
        return "" if value is None else str(value)

    def llm_change_direction(decision: ReviewDecision) -> str:
        reviewed = decision.source.is_machine and not decision.source.is_unreviewed
        if not reviewed or not decision.is_example:
            return ""
        if decision.status == DecisionStatus.DISCARDED:
            return "kept->discarded"
        if decision.status == DecisionStatus.KEPT:
            return "discarded->kept"
        return ""

    records = LinkedRecords(session)
    with open(output_path, "w", newline="", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        writer = csv.writer(f)
        if spreadsheet_safe:
            writer = SpreadsheetSafeWriter(writer, CSV_NUMERIC_COLUMNS)

        # Header row
        writer.writerow(
            [
                "status",
                "title",
                "authors",
                "year",
                "venue",
                "doi",
                "url",
                "tags",
                "abstract",
                "provider",
                "best_rank",
                "providers_count",
                "decision_source",
                "llm_confidence",
                "llm_review_outcome",
                "llm_change_direction",
                "source_relabelled",
                *LLM_AUDIT_FIELDS,
                *AGENT_AUDIT_FIELDS,
                *HUMAN_AUDIT_FIELDS,
                "reset_from",
                "abstract_from",
                "paper_id",
            ]
        )

        # Write all decisions
        for decision in session.decisions:
            paper = decision.paper
            place = relevance_place(decision, records)
            writer.writerow(
                [
                    decision.status.value,
                    paper.title,
                    "; ".join(paper.authors) if paper.authors else "",
                    paper.year or "",
                    paper.venue or "",
                    paper.doi or "",
                    paper.url or "",
                    "; ".join(decision.tags) if decision.tags else "",
                    paper.abstract or "",
                    decision.provider,
                    "" if place is None else place,
                    len(returning_databases(decision, records)),
                    decision.source.value,
                    (
                        f"{decision.llm_confidence:.3f}"
                        if decision.llm_confidence is not None
                        else ""
                    ),
                    llm_review_outcome(decision),
                    llm_change_direction(decision),
                    "; ".join(
                        f"{r.get('from')}->{r.get('to')} {r.get('at')}"
                        + (f" by {r['by']}" if r.get("by") else "")
                        for r in decision.relabelled
                    ),
                    *(classifier_cell(value) for value
                      in llm_audit_of(decision).values()),
                    *(value or "" for value
                      in agent_audit_of(decision).values()),
                    *(value or "" for value
                      in human_record_of(decision).values()),
                    "; ".join(
                        f"{r.get('status')} by {r.get('source')} "
                        f"{r.get('at')}"
                        + (f" by {r['by']}" if r.get("by") else "")
                        for r in decision.resets
                    ),
                    abstract_from_cell(decision),
                    get_paper_id(paper),
                ]
            )
